[Opening "English Opening: Symmetrical Variation, Ultra-Symmetrical Variation"]

{English Opening: Symmetrical Variation, Ultra-Symmetrical Variation. Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.}
1. c4 c5 2. g3 Nc6 3. Bg2 g6 4. Nc3 Bg7 5. a3 Nf6 {Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.} 6. Rb1 e6 7. b4 cxb4 8. axb4 ! d5 {Here the exchange is tempting and wrong: trading the good bishop leaves the dark squares bare.} (8... Nxb4 Ra1 Na2 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. b5 Ne5 10. cxd5 exd5 11. Nf3 Nxf3+ ?! 12. Bxf3 Bf5 13. d3 O-O 14. O-O Rc8 15. Bd2 d4 16. Na4 Qd7 17. Qb3 Bg4 18. Rfc1 Bxf3 19. exf3 b6 20. Kg2 Nd5 21. Rc4 Rce8 22. Bb4 Re2 23. Kg1 Rfe8 24. Rc2 Qxb5 25. Rxe2 Rxe2 26. Nc5 bxc5 27. Qxd5 Qxd3 28. Qd8+ Bf8 29. Bxc5 Qxb1+ 30. Kg2 {Resignation is timely: the king cannot be defended and the counterplay is one move too slow.} Rxf2+ 0-1

